It looks like the error object may not be getting passed correctly. Try updating the logError function in errorHandler.js to ensure it checks if the error object is defined before trying to access its properties. Here’s how you can modify it:

```javascript
function logError(error) {
    if (error && error.message) {
        console.error(`Error: ${error.message}`);
    } else {
        console.error('An unknown error occurred.');
    }
}
```
Also, ensure that whenever you call `logError`, the error object is properly passed from monitorService.js. After that, run your tests again with Jest to confirm it’s working correctly.
